  "plain": "This story is about a hidden planet far out in the solar system that was talked about and then dropped. Matt LaCroix, a researcher, says on Jesse Michels' podcast that in the 1990s NASA, the US space agency, spoke of something like a \"Planet 10.\" Then, he says, an astronomer named Myles Standish redid the maths and said, in effect, we made a mistake, forget about it. LaCroix tells it to suggest that the idea of a hidden planet was dismissed too quickly."
